# Architecture

Monorepo (PNPM workspaces):
- app/ — primary Nuxt application with frontend, server (Nitro/H3), Prisma schema/migrations, and tests
- microservice/ — companion Nitro/H3 service for specialized operational tasks (e.g., DB key rotation + migrate)
- scripts/, .deploy/, .github/ — automation, deployment templates, CI/CD workflows

## App (Nuxt) layout

- app/components, app/pages — Vue components and pages (Pinia stores in app/stores)
- app/plugins — Nuxt plugins (API client, store init, snapshot menu, etc.)
- app/middleware — front-end navigation guards (auth/admin)
- app/server — Nitro backend:
  - api/ — route files: REST-like endpoints by path and method suffix (.get.ts/.post.ts/...)
  - clients/ — prismaClient, redisClient, queuesClient, postmark/openai, nats
  - lib/ — shared server utilities (auth/session helpers, pagination, error mapping, etc.)
  - middleware/ — server middleware (auth, security headers, sitemap redirects)
  - services/ — domain and integration services (PlaidSync, TransactionMatching, Forecast, Reports, Notifications, etc.)
  - queues/ — BullMQ queue definitions (backup/plaid/recalculate)
  - cron/ — nuxt-cron entry points (daily/hourly tasks)
  - routes/ — non-API routes (e.g., health, sitemap, _nuxt forwarding)
- app/prisma — Prisma schema, migrations, generated reencryption helpers
- app/schema — Zod schemas shared by API/server logic
- app/lib — browser/server-shared utilities (formatting, sorting, rounding, etc.)
- app/tests — Playwright E2E, unit/integration tests; vitest configs

## Microservice layout

- microservice/server.ts — Nitro/H3 server bootstrap
- microservice/routes — minimal endpoints (e.g., migrate.get/post, test.get) used by operational flows
- microservice/clients — prisma/redis clients, matching app-side stack at a smaller scope
- microservice/lib/bull.ts — BullMQ support (when/if used here)
- microservice/prisma — dedicated schema subset + generated reencryption
- microservice/scripts/k8s-rotate-db-key.sh — GKE in-cluster key rotation helper

## Data access and encryption

- Prisma is the single ORM for both app and microservice; both target MySQL 8
- Field-level encryption via prisma-field-encryption (annotations in app/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Generated reencrypt migrators under app/prisma/reencrypt/* (and microservice equivalent)

## Background processing

- Redis + BullMQ: app/server/queues/* define queues for backup, Plaid sync, and forecast recalculation
- nuxt-cron: app/server/cron/* define scheduled jobs (hourly/daily) to enqueue work

## Forecast engine

- app/server/services/forecast/* contains a modular engine:
  - ForecastEngine orchestrates services (DataLoaderService, AccountRegisterService, ReoccurrenceService, RegisterEntryService, LoanCalculatorService, TransferService, DateTime/ModernCacheService, DataPersisterService)
  - Tests are extensive under app/server/services/forecast/__tests__

## How pieces fit together

- Frontend → useAPI/useAppFetch composables → call Nitro API routes under app/server/api
- API routes → validate (Zod), auth/middleware, delegate to app/server/services/*
- Services → read/write via server/clients/prismaClient.ts (with encryption plugin) and redisClient.ts
- Heavy/periodic tasks → queues via server/queues/* and scheduled by server/cron/*
- Microservice is deployed alongside the app and used by operational flows (e.g., nightly/staging DB key rotation calling microservice /migrate, then rolling deploys)
